@startuml
title Map & Browse Flow - Public Shelter List + Leaflet Map (M4)

actor Visitor

participant "MapPage" as MP
participant "ShelterGateway" as SG
participant "ApiClient" as AC
participant "LeafletService" as LS
participant "Router" as R
database "Spring Boot /api/shelters" as API

== Default route: /map ==
note over MP
  Public - no auth. GET /api/shelters?source=ALL returns every
  ACTIVE shelter (registry + user) - auto-hidden shelters (the 5th
  community "does not exist" report) are absent from the public
  list. Estonia-scale data (hundreds) - the backend deliberately
  has no paging yet (fetch-all is fine).
end note
Visitor -> MP : open /map
MP -> SG : list(ALL)
SG -> AC : get<ShelterDto[]>('/api/shelters?source=ALL')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters?source=ALL
API --> AC : ShelterDto[]
AC --> SG : typed array
SG --> MP : models
MP -> LS : renderShelters(shelters)
note over LS
  leaflet map centered on Estonia (lat ~58.6, lng ~25.0, zoom 7).
  One L.marker per shelter; markers for USER vs REGISTRY sources
  get distinct icons; no clustering needed at this scale.
  Reported state (nonexistentReports > 0) OVERRIDES the provenance
  colours: the single orange marker (the --color-reported token)
  with the third legend entry (Registry / User-submitted / Reported).
end note
LS --> MP : markers layer ready
MP --> Visitor : map + sidebar list

== Source filter ==
Visitor -> MP : click "Registry / User / All" chip
MP -> SG : list(REGISTRY)   ' server-side filter
SG -> AC : get<ShelterDto[]>('/api/shelters?source=REGISTRY')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters?source=REGISTRY
API --> AC : ShelterDto[]
SG --> MP : models
MP -> LS : replaceMarkers(shelters)
LS --> MP : updated
MP --> Visitor : filtered markers

== Trust filters (composable with source) ==
note over MP
  The trust-filter row under the source chips: a "Reviewed" toggle
  (reviewed=true), a "Has capacity" toggle (hasCapacity=true) and a
  Rating select ("Any rating" = no param / "1+".."5+" = minRating 1..5).
  Every combination composes with the source chip - each change is the
  same SERVER refetch + list rebuild, never client-side filtering.
  Rows render the shared trust badges: the "Reported" badge, the
  status-flag text ("Reported closed" / "Confirmed open") and the
  occupancy text (firm or hedged band + recency) - only when the DTO
  carries the state, never client-derived.
end note
Visitor -> MP : toggle "Reviewed" / "Has capacity" or pick "4+"
MP -> SG : list(ALL, {reviewed: true, minRating: 4})   ' server-side trust filter
SG -> AC : get<ShelterDto[]>('/api/shelters?reviewed=true&minRating=4')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters?reviewed=true&minRating=4
API --> AC : ShelterDto[]
SG --> MP : models
MP -> LS : replaceMarkers(shelters)
LS --> MP : updated
MP --> Visitor : filtered markers + rows with trust badges

== Error / empty handling ==
alt backend unreachable
  API --> AC : connection error
  AC --> MP : ApiError (network)
  MP --> Visitor : banner "map unavailable - is the backend running?"
else zero shelters
  API --> AC : []
  MP --> Visitor : empty state "no shelters yet"
end

== Select (zoom in, stay on /map) ==
Visitor -> MP : click marker (or list row)
' street level (SHELTER_ZOOM)
MP -> LS : flyTo(lat, lng, 16)
LS --> MP : map zoomed on the shelter
MP --> Visitor : shelter selected + highlighted (sidebar row)

== Open detail (explicit step) ==
Visitor -> MP : click "View details" on the selected row
MP -> R : navigate('/shelters', id)
R --> : ShelterDetailPage (M5)

note over MP
  M4 keeps the list/map read-only. Submission ("+ Add shelter"),
  detail and reviews arrive in M5 (verified accounts only).
end note
@enduml
